From e12d298399fa5af2a1ef04370d03144bb7fe94a1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: MasherDon <62326358+MasherDon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 04 Nov 2026 04:22:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 106/112] llama : SiegeLadder P19 stage A - layer-major
 prefill, off by default (LLAMA_DSV4_LAYER_MAJOR=k,
 LLAMA_DSV4_LAYER_MAJOR_GIB=8)

V4.1 only. A prompt call of two or more ubatches (one sequence, causal, no embeddings, n_rs_seq 0) runs "group of k
layers -> every ubatch of a superchunk" instead of "ubatch -> all layers"; groups break at the first decoder layer (20),
superchunks hold what the ubatches carry within the GiB budget. Every graph (group, ubatch) computes what the whole
graph did on the same data with the same P11 wave plan, so the output is the same byte for byte.

- KV: a metadata pass applies every ubatch once and snapshots the DSV4 contexts (raw ring cells, base / swa indices,
  comp i_cur / n_kv); lm_seek(u) restores ubatch u before each graph (llama-kv-cache-dsv4, llama-kv-cache seek / snap).
- Graph (deepseek4): layers [lm_l0, lm_l1); a segment past layer 0 takes the stream, the mix, the top-k and the
  candidate verdicts as inputs in the shapes and types the segment before exported; computed exports are graph outputs,
  a segment's own input (or C7c's view of it) stays host-side; past the cut only the positions are cut; C14 never
  crosses a segment; graph_last_moe is the segment's last MoE layer (P4: the encoder's last); P4's group ends without
  an export.
- Context: per-ubatch slots with separate in / out carries, a pinned host buffer per item grown by ggml_nbytes; set
  only for inputs the segment's graph allocated; graph reuse off for segments (allow_reuse compares the bounds);
  outputs and n_tokens_prev in the last group (P4: its group); the scheduler's sync inside the loop.
- Inputs: the C7 raw mask is built directly when a decoder-only segment has no plain mask; P13 rows / mask / C7 mask
  are each filled when present; engram's eager path skips layers outside the segment.

Checked (SiegeLadder queue105, bench/p19_check.py, llama-logits --score-file, consult C text 32 000 + 16 tokens,
-ub 2048, RAM tier 40 GiB): k = 1 and k = 4 equal k = 0 byte for byte at all 16 target positions in exact and in
default without drops (P4 and the C7c cut exercised). Drafted by Cursor (composer-2.5) in SiegeLadder lab card L019,
fixed by the lead.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
